@prabhat-kumar96 after further investigation: it doesn't work for me because I am on an `arm64` machine and we use [a console version of `gvproxy`](https://github.com/containers/gvisor-tap-vsock/blob/94849c1a06a280c0bbc38b09fea727a3eb07009e/Makefile#L69) on `arm64` machines (and a [GUI version for `amd64`](https://github.com/containers/gvisor-tap-vsock/blob/94849c1a06a280c0bbc38b09fea727a3eb07009e/Makefile#L35)). It works if I use [this version of gvproxy](https://github.com/containers/gvisor-tap-vsock/releases/download/v0.8.9/gvproxy-arm64.exe). This is a bug in the function `Win-SSHProxy` of `winmake.ps1` where we should pull ~~`gvproxy-windows-arm64.exe`~~ `gvproxy-arm64.exe` rather than ~~`gvproxy-arm64.exe`~~ `gvproxy-windows-arm64.exe`. Would you mind updating your PR with this fix?

Also, for the `SysProcAttr` used to run `podman machine server9p`: it's a console application and it's safer to use `windows.CREATE_NO_WINDOW` as we already do [when running wsl commands](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/3c010e5653cda81270cabf52614e042b3925da3e/pkg/machine/wsl/wutil/wutil.go#L41). See [this article](https://ikriv.com/dev/cpp/ConsoleProxy/flags) for reference.

To be on the safe side, I would update the start of [gvproxy ](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/3c010e5653cda81270cabf52614e042b3925da3e/pkg/machine/shim/networking.go#L86) and [win-sshproxy](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/3c010e5653cda81270cabf52614e042b3925da3e/pkg/machine/machine_windows.go#L174) too. And use the `DETACHED_PROCESS` `SysProcAttr`, as you did for `podman machine server9p`, because that's the right thing to do for GUI apps.
